TOKEN tinybird_read READ

DESCRIPTION >
    Estimated price of one agent call, per agent.

    An agent call's generations - model steps and MCP tool calls - all carry the
    id of the request that minted their run token, so grouping by it reassembles
    the call. The parent row is free, so cost is the sum over its children.

    Median and p90 rather than a mean: a run that enters a tool loop costs a
    multiple of one that answers directly, and an average hides that.

NODE runs
DESCRIPTION >
    One row per agent call. Non-final rows are fallback attempts with no price,
    so excluding them keeps `calls` a count of generations, not attempts.
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        agent_id,
        parent_request_id,
        sum(total_price) AS run_price,
        count() AS calls
    FROM generation_event_v2
    WHERE
        parent_request_id != ''
        AND is_final
        AND environment = {{String(environment, 'production')}}
        AND start_time >= now() - INTERVAL {{Int32(days, 7)}} DAY
        {% if defined(agent_id) %}
        AND agent_id = {{String(agent_id)}}
        {% end %}
    GROUP BY agent_id, parent_request_id

NODE endpoint
SQL >
    SELECT
        agent_id,
        count() AS runs,
        round(median(run_price), 6) AS median_price,
        round(quantile(0.9)(run_price), 6) AS p90_price,
        round(avg(run_price), 6) AS avg_price,
        round(avg(calls), 2) AS avg_calls
    FROM runs
    GROUP BY agent_id
    ORDER BY runs DESC
